<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ monopolies panel clears Powerco electricity buy.</title>
<headline>NZ monopolies panel clears Powerco electricity buy.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's monopolies panel, the Commerce Commission, on Monday authorised electricity company Powerco's proposed acquisition of Egmonst Electricity.</p>
<p>In a statement the commission said it was satisfied that the public benefits from the deal would outweigh the detriments in terms of dominance being acquired or strengthened.  </p>
<p>Industry observers have predicted the link-up, which is estimated to carry a NZ$124 million price tag, may lead to further consolidation moves in the regional power market.</p>
<p>Egmont is owed by a local regional council, while Powerco is currently unlisted.</p>
